From: blackhat-7 <44942105+blackhat-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:46:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 04/33] i-quant signs and IQ4 table lookups with v_perm on HIP

Port of opt7/integrate d17c9e38 3acec79d onto v0.2.9: the IQ2/IQ3 sign step as v_perm_b32 byte selects
(iq_signs.cuh) instead of the emulated __vcmpne4 / __vsub4, and the IQ4 codebook lookups in the v_perm form on every
HIP target. Bitwise the old form on every codebook word (tests/hip/iq_signs.cu, target hip_iq_signs). v0.2.9's
staged sign-mask tables (STRATA_IQ_STAGE_TABLES, opt-in) keep their own path.
Measured on 0.1.43: expert kernels -12 to -16% (real weights, T=1-4), GPU rings -0.3 to -0.6 ms a round.
